From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:44:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): Termux-style extra-keys row for the terminal on
 touch devices

Carried from upstream PR omnigent-ai/omnigent#6136 (btli), squashed from
its head d2c80fe8 so we can use it on a phone before it merges. It adds
Esc / Tab / Shift+Tab / arrows / PgUp / PgDn and sticky Ctrl, Alt and Shift
under the terminal, with a Touch & mobile setting (Auto / Always / Never).

The PR head includes the two iOS fixes we suggested on it: touchend is
cancelled on the row so the soft keyboard stays up, and the row keeps the
bottom safe-area padding unless a docked keyboard covers the home
indicator. The web code matches the PR head; the only addition is the
`touch-keys` entry in feature-map/terminals.md.

Not ours to upstream: drop this commit when #6136 lands.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
